{"condition": "evidence", "constrained_a": false, "id": "svb-716f0a9027bd", "input_tokens": 579, "input_truncated": false, "max_new_tokens": 128, "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_key": "qwen-1.5b", "model_revision": "989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306", "output_reached_token_limit": false, "output_tokens": 105, "prompt_sha256": "4a3bf2764eab1a2b3995942a468eacca00da2875d13070f755eb9a1f8ae0b01c", "raw_text": "The supplied record establishes that the body weight of chick 1 increased from 42 grams at birth to 205 grams on day 21 while receiving diet 1. It does not establish whether these changes occurred due to the specific effects of diet 1 alone, nor does it provide information about other factors influencing chick growth such as nutrition, environment, or genetics. The data shows only one observation per day, which limits the ability to draw broader conclusions about overall growth patterns or potential interactions between different variables.", "seconds": 31.383649065999634, "status": "completed", "task": "B"}
{"condition": "evidence", "constrained_a": false, "id": "svb-e3d611a0ffa3", "input_tokens": 581, "input_truncated": false, "max_new_tokens": 128, "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_key": "qwen-1.5b", "model_revision": "989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306", "output_reached_token_limit": true, "output_tokens": 128, "prompt_sha256": "a6e7bbf94b92edf4bf814a1814683610ac50f3194c5f17c76d8dc7890c958292", "raw_text": "The supplied record establishes that chick 1's growth series indicates that diet 1 caused exactly 163 grams of additional body weight compared to what this chick would have gained without diet 1. However, it does not establish causation between diet 1 and the specific increase in weight of 163 grams. The record only shows the relationship between diet and overall growth but does not specify which individual weight change corresponds to the 163 gram difference. Therefore, while the data supports a general trend towards increased weight due to diet 1, it cannot pinpoint the exact cause-and-effect relationship for the 163 gram", "seconds": 36.73410483800035, "status": "completed", "task": "B"}
{"condition": "evidence", "constrained_a": false, "id": "svb-db97426ec44e", "input_tokens": 416, "input_truncated": false, "max_new_tokens": 128, "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_key": "qwen-1.5b", "model_revision": "989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306", "output_reached_token_limit": false, "output_tokens": 124, "prompt_sha256": "39376c217ddd3682056106aa5ab9c94933c4d36dcf5ce542000a0475e0da7810", "raw_text": "The supplied record establishes that the recorded oxygen-demand values decreased between day 3 and day 4. It provides the observed data points: day 3 has a value of 19 mg/l and day 4 has a value of 16 mg/l. However, it does not provide information about the method used to measure these values or whether there were any systematic errors or changes over time that could affect the accuracy of the measurements. Therefore, while the record supports the claim that the oxygen-demand values decreased, it cannot be definitively concluded that this was due solely to a change in the measured values themselves.", "seconds": 33.3377761030024, "status": "completed", "task": "B"}
